# Whitelist build context.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and Docker does NOT read .gitignore — so
# without this file the build ships the whole working tree (local research
# data, output/, .git, caches) instead of the tracked source. Ignore everything, then re-admit only what `pip install -e .` needs.
#
# Adding a new top-level file the build needs? Add a matching `!` line below.

*

!learnm8/
!tests/
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!.coveragerc

# Needed by Dockerfile.base — it is the single source of truth for the conda env.
!environment.yml

# Re-exclude junk that would otherwise ride along inside the un-ignored dirs.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/.cache/
**/*.h5
**/*.parquet
**/*.bak
